<http://data.silknow.org/object/01a8b794-0b48-3ee8-bf90-df346ca1acf0/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Woven furnishing textile sample with a blue background with a bold pattern of a white leaf merging into a large open flower, above which a group of smaller flowers intertwine their stems. The veins of the flowers and leaves are outlined in sage green. The fabric is woven in silk and wool with a half-drop repeat. The left side has a <sup>1/2\"</sup> selvedge whilst the other edges are bound with machine stitching. Four brass rings are inset along the top, and a label is stuck on the lower right hand corner, inscribed '81 661 A'. A small patch of similar weave with a green background and sandy brown outlines is tacked onto the back."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/01a8b794-0b48-3ee8-bf90-df346ca1acf0> .

